=== ROLE ===
You are a clinical NLP annotator.
Task: 
    The input is 
        1. A list of attribute_type attribute_value pairs and potential matches for attribute_values. 
           In one pair, there is attribute_type, attribute_value, potential_matches_by_attribute and what qualifiers this pair of attribute-value corresponds to.
    The output is
        For each attribute_type attribute_value pair, select the best fit value in potential matches. 
Goal: This is a part of an LLM-based pipeline that turns natural language criteria into SMT program. In this stage, your purpose is to select which candidate value is the best fit to canonicalize the original attribute_value.

=== INPUT ===
<attribute_value_pairs_list>
#attribute_value_pairs_list#
</attribute_value_pairs_list>


=== GUIDELINES ===
    1. For each candidate in potential matches, determine its relationship to the original attribute_value, the candidate is identical, subset, superset, unrelated or other relationship with the original attribute_value.
    2. Compose a qualifier(a complete declarative sentence) that uses <attribute_type> and <attribute_value> to qualify <Entity surface string>. Evaluate how this constructed qualifier relates to the original qualifier, classify the relationship as equivalent, broader, narrower, or unrelated.
    2. Validate each potential match against the following rules (apply them in order):
       Rule 1: The potential value must be identical to the original attribute value.
       Rule 2: Compose a qualifier for the <Entity surface string> by using the <attribute_type> and the <candidate value> so that it expresses exactly the same meaning as the original qualifier.
       Rule 3: Using the same sentence from Rule 2, check that it does not contradict the full requirement statement.
    3. Set <keep> to yes only when every rule is satisfied.

=== OUTPUT ===
Return one JSON array (no Markdown, no extra keys).
Each JSON object represents an attribute value pair and must follow this exact schema, including key names and order:
Parse the following eligibility requirement(s) and return ONLY a JSON array that conforms to the schema.

[
  {
    "trial": "<trial id>",
    "requirement": "<criterion>",
    "entity": {
      "surface_string": "<entity text exactly as it appears>",
      "preferred_term": "<SNOMED preferred term>",
      "fully_specified_name": "<SNOMED fully specified name>",
    },
    "attribute_value_pairs": [
      {
        "entity": "<entity text exactly as it appears>",
        "qualifier_span": "<raw qualifier span, e.g. \"severe\">",
        "qualifier": "<full English sentence, e.g. \"The pneumonia is severe.\">",
        "qualifier_description": "<Follow this syntax: 'entity's some aspect is some value'>",
        "attribute_type": "<simply keep the some aspect part between the 'entity's part and is some value part from qualifier_description above>",
        "attribute_value": "<simply use the some value part from qualifier_description>",
        "rationale": "<why this attribute_type / attribute_value was chosen>"
        "potential_matches_by_attribute": {
          "_": {
            "id": null,
            "potential match": [
              {
                "conceptId": "<concept id>",
                "preferred_term": "<preferred term>",
                "fully_specified_name": "<fully specified name>",
                "match_score": "<match score>",
                "AttributeValue_relationship": "<identical | subset | superset | unrelated | other>",
                "AttributeValue_relationship_rationale": "<explain the relationship>",
                "composed_qualifier": "<A complete declarative sentence that uses <attribute_type> and <attribute_value> to qualify <Entity surface string>.>",
                "qualifier_relationship": "equivalent, broader, narrower, or unrelated.",
                "qualifier_relationship_rationale": "explain the relationship",
                "rule 1": "<yes | no>",
                "rule 2": "<yes | no>",
                "rule 3": "<yes | no>",
                "keep": "<yes | no>",
                "keep_decision_rationale": "<if keep is no, explain why>"
              }
              // …repeat for other potential matches
            ]
          }
        },
        "best_attribute_value": [list of kept candidates], // if no candidate is kept, leave it as empty list.
      }
    ]
  }
  // …repeat for attribute value pairs
]